  "notes": "Both sides are a single linear pass over the agents, so both scale ~n; neither is a solver race. WITHOUT's median is a frozen-label frame (stream only; 100 of every 125 frames), its p95 is a relabel frame (hub at rest) that costs about what WITH costs every frame. WITH = recompute the optimal power-cell labels every frame (exactly optimal by Lemma cells:optimality; any classical power-cell labeller gives the same labels). Quality is load-independent in exact terms (mis-routed fraction a/4 = 11.25%, cost excess a^2/12 at a=0.45); the sampled values converge to it as n grows. The paper's actual result (RMS map change ~ W2^(1/3), sharp) is a sensitivity warning about how many agents the optimal assignment reshuffles, not a speedup. Single thread on both sides; 1 frame = label pass + streaming every 4th agent."
